#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Make spw init runtime-aware so it provisions a portable base scaffold everywhere, augments from checkout-native assets when available, and stops assuming source-tree-relative paths."
 ~#taste: "correctness, clarity, portability, layering"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-20 18:34] observe — packages/spw-cli/src/init.ts still derives workbenchRoot from the source tree layout, which becomes incorrect once the CLI is bundled into dist/bin or published as a tarball.
 >>[2026-03-20 18:35] observe — the copied commit-review skill is not universally portable; it expects repo-local support scripts, so packaged/bootstrap behavior must be explicit about what it can and cannot provision.
 >>[2026-03-20 18:35] decide — this slice should make runtime context structural: detect package root, provision a portable base scaffold first, augment from checkout assets when present, and degrade truthfully instead of pretending every init target is a full workbench clone.
 >>[2026-03-20 18:35] taste — the boutique-quality bar here is honest affordance signaling and portability; bootstrap flows should reveal their runtime posture instead of hiding it behind brittle relative paths.
 >>[2026-03-20 18:39] revise — user raised portability and interoperability explicitly, so the plan now prefers portable templates over direct copying of repo-bound affordances wherever possible.
 >>[2026-03-20 18:35] hygiene — worktree is clean on main@df7a32c6b10612f53b6cfbdb6aa6ff6a420aa6bf; no unrelated drift to split.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[support-shape]: "Which affordances belong in the portable base scaffold versus the optional workbench-specific augmentation layer?"
}

